## Resolution

- `nrl-repr::pruning` implements f64 weight/activation energy and allocation-free stable heap selection. `nrl_lab::prune` packs the original rows/columns; `linear_spline_control` preserves the same mapping and projections.
- Block schema 1 records retained channels and refuses schema 0 explicitly. This is not a full source-identity/provenance manifest.
- At bd583103, after fast-test staging bb0a5750, `bash nrl/tools/check.sh` passed **16 host tests**, both portable release rlibs, and three differential/train/round-trip fixture cases on the NRL branch. No tests ran on fast-test.
- The external fixture regenerated byte for byte (SHA-256 28c8ddf016cd57dd4bbb5f91a9b9e0ab9e7b6b7502c31c5275937248178a9f7f). Maximum recorded block/gradient error was 2.842170943040401e-14, within the declared tolerances.
- Reports: `nrl/reports/pruning-f64-2026-10-26.json` and `pruning-check-2026-10-26.txt`. No trained-model improvement or native execution is claimed. Cubic Hermite, SVD and the general model pipeline remain under 900.
